*9/3/86 Merged Henry Nusbacher and Jeff Honig's updates (having  [1.24]
*       update identifiers of "FIXUP" and "CCT001") as update--->[1.24]
INTERNET TITLE 'CUCCA VM NETWORK MAILER VERSION 1 - DEFAULT RSCS ROUTIN*
               G EXIT + INTERNET GATEWAY HANDLER'
         MACRO
&LABEL   BSP   &RX
         LCLC  &L
&L       SETC  'B&SYSNDX'
         AIF   ('&LABEL' EQ '').NOLABEL
&L       SETC  '&LABEL'
.NOLABEL ANOP
&L       CLI   0(&RX),C' '         IS THIS A BLANK ?
         BNE   A&SYSNDX            NOPE, CONTINUE
         BCTR  &RX,0               ELSE, BUMP BACKWARD BY 1
         B     &L                  AND CHECK PREVIOUS CHARACTER
A&SYSNDX LA    &RX,1(,&RX)         RX -> FIRST BLANK
         MEND
         MACRO
&LABEL   GATE  &NAME,&NODE,&USER,&FLAG=*-*,&PATH=*-*
&LABEL   DC    CL16'&NAME'         NAME OF DOMAIN
         DC    CL8'&NODE'          NAME OF GATEWAY NODE
         DC    CL8'&USER'          NAME OF GATEWAY USERID
         DC    A(&PATH)            INDIRECT PATH DATA
         DC    AL1(&FLAG)          FLAG DATA
         DC    AL3(0)              ROUND OUT TO A FULL WORD
         MEND
         EJECT ,
INTERNET CSECT ,
* INTERNET -
*  This routine punches individual files to RSCS sites that are
*  either not running this Mailer or are running a different
*  mailer that doesn't know how to handle the same message for
*  several recipients as one file.
*
*  This routine has been updated to handle internet mail.  If a
*  mail file arrives with the final characters specifying a domain
*  like - .UUCP, .ARPA, .CCNET, .BITNET, .MAILNET
*  then handle it.  Some get BSMTP envelopes while others don't.
*
*  Changed logic for domain addressing.  A domain suffix is
*  located if present and then looked up in a table.  The table
*  specifies the routine to process the specified domain.  If
*  no domain address is found, control passes to old DEFRT code.
*  If an unknown domain address is found, an error message is
*  printed.
*
*  A complete list of gateways is contained in GATEWAY MEMOI   FIXUP
*  that is available from Nicserve or Netserv.                 FIXUP
*
         EJECT ,
*  History:
*
*  DEFRT was written by Alan Crosswell (EACUS@CUVMB) in 4/82.
*  BSMTP was written by Arti Ecock (ECKCU@CUNYVM) in 3/84.
*  These two programs were merged together by Henry Nussbacher
*  (VSHANK@WEIZMANN) in 2/85 to form the base INTERNET program.
*  The code has undergone changes by the following people:
*
*  05/24/85 BY Reg Quinton      (A362@UWOCC1)
*  06/10/85 BY Jeffrey Honig    (NETMAINT@CLVM)
*  07/16/85 BY Henry Nussbacher
*  09/05/85 BY Jeffrey Honig
*  09/11/85 BY Henry Nussbacher
*  09/19/85 BY Henry Nussbacher
*  10/30/85 BY Reg Quinton
*  12/11/85 BY Henry Nussbacher
*  01/12/86 BY Jeffrey C Honig                                 CCT001
*  01/29/87 BY Henry Nussbacher
*
* Modifications:
*
* This release represents a new base level for INTERNET.  All
* people who wish to make modifications and enhancements are
* urged to do so, but only in standard CMS Update format.
* Please use, XEDIT INTERNET ASSEMBLE (CTL INTERNET SID updtname
* to create your updates and VMFASM to assemble them.  Changes will
* be accepted into INTERNET under the following 3 conditions:
*
* 1) They arrive in standard CMS Update format
* 2) They assemble correctly into the most current version of
*    INTERNET
* 3) They have been checked and verified by the author to perform
*    as stated
*
* These changes should be sent to me (Vshank@Weizmann).
*
* CCT001:                                                      CCT001
*   Added 'RETURN' parameter (to be specified in MAILER        CCT001
* PROFILE).  When specified will cause mail without domain     CCT001
* addresses to be returned to the originating user with        CCT001
* an 'Unknown Host:' message.                                  CCT001
*                                                              CCT001
* Changed message 'Syntax Error in field- Unknown Domain' to   CCT001
* 'Unknown Domain'.  Requires associated mods in MSGTEXT       CCT001
* ASSEMBLE for message 51.                                     CCT001
*
* Installation:
*
* To install the latest version of the INTERNET exit:
*
* 1) Edit the table of gateways listed near the end.  Some domains
*    have multiple gateways.  Choose only one gateway per domain.
*    Example: you could choose the Uwocc1 gateway to UUCP if you
*    were in Canada or the Psuvax1 gateway if your node is closer
*    to Psuvax1.
* 2) VMFASM INTERNET INTERNET
* 3) TXTLIB DEL MAILER INTERNET
* 4) TXTLIB ADD MAILER INTERNET
* 5) Restart your mailer
*
         EJECT ,
PAB      DSECT ,
@MBLOK   DS    F             ADDRESS OF MAILBLOK
@ACT     DS    F             ADDRESS OF ACTADR BLOCK
* REGISTER USAGE -
R0  EQU  0 -
R1  EQU  1 -
R2  EQU  2 -
R3  EQU  3 -
R4  EQU  4 -
R5  EQU  5 -
R6  EQU  6 -
R7  EQU  7 -
R8  EQU  8 -
R9  EQU  9 -
R10 EQU 10 - ACTADR BASE
R11 EQU 11 - MAILBLOK BASE
R12 EQU 12 - PROGRAM BASE
R13 EQU 13 - SAVE AREA
R14 EQU 14 - SUBROUTINE LINKAGE
R15 EQU 15 - SUBROUTINE LINKAGE
         BLOCKS ,
         MAILBLOK ,
         EJECT ,
         PRINT NOGEN
         PUNCH 'SPB'            TELL LOADER TO START ON NEW PAGE
INTERNET CSECT ,
         SAVE  (14,12),,*        SAVE CALLER'S REGISTERS
         USING INTERNET,R15      SET UP TEMP ADDRESSABILITY
         CNOP  0,4               ALIGN SAVE AREA TO FULLWORD
         BAL   R15,*+76          BRANCH AROUND LOCAL SAVE AREA
         DROP  R15               DROP TEMP BASE REGISTER
         USING SAVEAREA,R13,R12  SET UP NEW BASE REGISTERS
SAVEAREA DC    18F'-1'           REGISTER SAVE AREA
*        GRAB A 2ND BASE REGISTER BEFORE SOME DODO TAKES IT
         ST    R15,8(,R13)       CHAIN FORWARD SAVE AREA PTR
         ST    R13,4(,R15)       CHAIN BACKWARD SAVE AREA PTR
         LR    R13,R15           LOAD UP THE BASE REGISTER
         LA    R12,4095(,R13)    LOAD SECOND BASE REGISTER
         LA    R12,1(,R12)       EVEN UP FOR 8K ADDRESSABILITY
         USING PAB,R1            PARMS
         L     R11,@MBLOK        GET MAILBLOK BASE
         L     R10,@ACT          GET ACTADR BASE
         USING MAILBLOK,R11
         USING ACTADR,R10
         MVI   FLAGS,0           CLEAR OPTIONS FLAG
         EJECT ,
         L     R7,ACTMBOX        GET MBOX BLOCK
         USING MBOX,R7         GET USER LIST
         L     R7,MBXDML         POINT TO HOST LIST
         USING NODE,R7         ADDRESS IT
         L     R7,NODDOWN        GET DOWN POINTER
         USING TOKEND,R7         ADDRESS THE HOST NAME TOKEN
         SR    R4,R4             GET ZERO
         L     R4,TOKLEN         LENGTH OF NODE STRING
         L     R3,TOKPTR
         LA    R2,WORK           POINT TO WORK AREA
         MVI   0(R2),C' '        SET UP FOR BUFFER CLEAR
         MVC   1(L'WORK-1,R2),0(R2)  PROPOGATE THE BLANK
         LR    R5,R4             LOAD UP LENGTH OF STRING
         BCTR  R5,0              -1 FOR EX
         EX    R5,COPY           AND MOVE THE ENTIRE STRING TO WORK
         EX    R5,UPIT           AND UPPERCASE IT FOR COMPARE
*        ADD LENGTH OF STRING TO START OF STRING
         LA    R3,WORK           POINT TO START OF DESTINATION
         AR    R3,R4             ADD IN LENGTH OF STRING
*        ALLOW FOR A 1 CHARACTER INTERNET NAME SO BACKUP TWO
         S     R3,=A(2)          BACKUP TO SHORTEST POSSIBLE
         LA    R1,8              SCAN BACKWARDS 8 CHARACTERS
DOTLOOP2 CLI   0(R3),C'.'        CHECK FOR BEGINNING OF DOMAIN
         BE    HAVEDOT2          FOUND IT!
         BCTR  R3,0              BACK UP TO PREVIOUS CHARACTER
         BCT   R1,DOTLOOP2       KEEP LOOKING
         B     UNKNOWN           NO DOMAIN NAME, USE DEFAULT EXCCT001
HAVEDOT2 EQU   *                 WE HAVE A FIRST DOT, KEEP SCANNING
         S     R3,=A(2)          BACKUP ANOTHER 2 SPOTS
         LA    R1,7              SCAN BACK AN ADDITIONAL 8
DOTLOOP1 CLI   0(R3),C'.'        HAVE WE HIT ANOTHER '.'?
         BE    HAVEDOT1          YES!!!  LET'S SEE IF IT HAS AN ENTRY
         BCTR  R3,0              BACK UP TO PREVIOUS CHARACTER
         BCT   R1,DOTLOOP1       AND KEEP LOOPING
*        IF WE DROP TO HERE, WE DID NOT FIND THE 2ND DOT AND HAVE TO
*        NOW SCAN FORWARD TO THE FIRST DOT WE FOUND.
SCANFWD  EQU   *
         LA    R3,1(,R3)         SCAN FORWARDS IN NODENAME
         CLI   0(R3),C'.'        HAVE WE HIT OUR ORIGINAL DOT?
         BNE   SCANFWD           NOPE, KEEP GOING FORWARD
         B     HAVEDOT           AND BRANCH TO SINGLE DOMAIN TABLE
         SPACE 3
HAVEDOT1 EQU   *
         LA    R3,1(,R3)         BUMP PAST DOT TO START OF NAME
         LA    R1,GATES1         POINT TO START OF TABLE
         LA    R6,GATESIZE       GET SIZE OF ENTRY
         LA    R7,GATES1ND       POINT TO END OF TABLE
         USING GATESECT,R1       SET UP ADDRESSABILITY FOR ENTRIES
GLOOP1   CLC   GATENAME,0(R3)    IS THIS THE DOMAIN WE WANT?
         BE    HAVEGATE          YES - SET UP AND GO PROCESS
         BXLE  R1,R6,GLOOP1      CONTINUE SCANING
*        DOMAIN NOT FOUND IN 2 LEVEL DOMAIN TABLE - GO TRY 1 LEVEL
         B     SCANFWD
         SPACE 3
HAVEDOT  EQU   *
         LA    R3,1(,R3)         BUMP PAST DOT TO START OF NAME
         LA    R1,GATES2         POINT TO START OF TABLE
         LA    R6,GATESIZE       GET SIZE OF ENTRY
         LA    R7,GATES2ND       POINT TO END OF TABLE
         USING GATESECT,R1       SET UP ADDRESSABILITY FOR ENTRIES
GLOOP    CLC   GATENAME,0(R3)    IS THIS THE DOMAIN WE WANT?
         BE    HAVEGATE          YES - SET UP AND GO PROCESS
         BXLE  R1,R6,GLOOP       CONTINUE SCANING
         LOG   INT051,(CA,(R3))                                CCT001
         LA    R15,8             INDICATE INVALID
         B     RET
         EJECT ,
HAVEGATE MVC   FLAGS,GATEFLAG    SET THE FLAG BYTE
         MVI   SEP,C'@'          MOVE IN DEFAULT SEPERATOR
         TM    FLAGS,INDIRECT    IS IT AN INDIRECT PATH?
         BZ    SKIPSEP           NOPE, SKIP THE '%' STUFFING
         MVI   SEP,C'%'          MOVE IN '%' SIGN
SKIPSEP  EQU   *
         MVC   TAGHOST(8),GATENODE  MOVE IN BITNET NODEID
         MVC   NETHOST(8),GATENODE  MOVE IN BITNET NODEID
         MVC   TAGUSER(8),GATEUSER  AND WHO TO SEND IT TO
         L     R1,GATEPATH       POINT TO THE PATH DATA
         DROP  R1                DROP ADDRESSABILITY
         TM    FLAGS,BSMTP       IS IT TO BE SENT BSMTP?
         BNZ   DO$BSMTP          YES, GO THERE
         B     DEFAULT           OTHERWISE SEND WITHOUT BSMTP
         EJECT ,
DO$BSMTP EQU   *
         L     R7,ACTMBOX        LOAD MBOX BASE REGISTER
         USING MBOX,R7         PROVIDE MBOX ADDRESSABILITY
*        FIRST BUILD THE "HELO NODENAME.BITNET" LINE
         LA    R2,WHOM           POINT TO RECEIVING FIELD
         MVI   0(R2),C' '        START BLANKING IT OUT
         MVC   1(L'WHOM-1,R2),0(R2)  PROPAGATE THE BLANK
         MVC   0(8,R2),MAILNODE  MOVE IN MY NODENAME
         LA    R2,8(,R2)         POINT PAST THE NODENAME
         BSP   R2                BACK UP TO LAST BLANK
         MVC   0(7,R2),=C'.BITNET'   FINISH OFF THE FIELD
*        NOW BUILD THE TICK LINE AND USE THE SPOOLID AS THE TICK
         MVC   TICK(4),MAILFTXT  MOVE IN SPOOLID "NNNN"
*        TIME TO BUILD THE "MAIL FROM:<USER@HOST.BITNET>" FIELD
         LA    R2,MADDR          POINT TO RECEIVING FIELD
         MVI   0(R2),C' '        SET UP FOR BUFFER CLEAR
         MVC   1(L'MADDR-1,R2),0(R2)  PROPOGATE THE BLANK
         MVC   0(8,R2),MAILUSER  COPY ORIGIN USERID
         LA    R8,8(,R2)         POINT PAST THE USERID
         BSP   R8                POINT TO FIRST BLANK
         MVI   0(R8),C'@'        MOVE AN "@"
         MVC   1(8,R8),MAILNODE  COPY THE ORIGIN HOST
         LA    R8,9(,R8)         POINT PAST THE HOST
         BSP   R8                POINT TO FIRST BLANK
         MVC   0(8,R8),=C'.BITNET>'  CLOSE THE FIELD
*        HERE, WE BUILD THE "RCPT TO:<INTERNET_ADDRESS>" FIELD
         L     R7,MBXLCL            POINT TO USER LIST
         USING NODE,R7         PROVIDE ADDRESSABILITY
         L     R7,NODDOWN        LOAD DOWN POINTER
         USING TOKEND,R7         ADDRESS THE USER NAME TOKEN
         SR    R4,R4             CLEAR A WORK REGISTER
         L     R4,TOKLEN         GET LENGTH OF USERID STRING
         CL    R4,=A(L'RADDR-1)  IS IT TOO LONG (<71)?
         BH    FAIL0             YES, FAIL
         BCTR  R4,0              LENGTH-1 FOR EXECUTE
         L     R3,TOKPTR         LOAD STRING ADDRESS
         LA    R2,RADDR          POINT TO RECEIVING FIELD
         MVI   0(R2),C' '        SET UP FOR BUFFER CLEAR
         MVC   1(L'RADDR-1,R2),0(R2)   PROPOGATE THE BLANK
         EX    R4,COPY           MVC 0(*-*,R2),0(R3)
         LA    R2,1(R2,R4)       POINT TO LAST CHARACTER
         MVC   0(1,R2),SEP       MOVE IN % OR @ OPERATOR
         LA    R2,1(,R2)         BUMP PAST THE % OR @
         LA    R3,L'RADDR        LOAD LENGTH OF FIELD
         SR    R3,R4             LOAD LENGTH OF FIELD LEFT-1
         L     R7,ACTMBOX        LOAD MBOX BASE REGISTER
         USING MBOX,R7         PROVIDE MBOX ADDRESSABILITY
         L     R7,MBXDML         POINT TO HOST LIST
         USING NODE,R7         PROVIDE ADDRESSABILITY
         L     R7,NODDOWN        LOAD DOWN POINTER
         USING TOKEND,R7         ADDRESS THE HOST NAME TOKEN
         SR    R4,R4             CLEAR A WORK REGISTER
         L     R4,TOKLEN         GET LENGTH OF HOST STRING
         CR    R4,R3             IS IT TOO LONG ?
         BH    FAIL0             YES, FAIL
         BCTR  R4,0              LENGTH-1 FOR EXECUTE
         L     R3,TOKPTR         LOAD STRING ADDRESS
         EX    R4,COPY           MVC 0(*-*,R2),0(R3)
         LA    R2,1(R2,R4)       POINT TO LAST CHARACTER
         TM    FLAGS,INDIRECT    GOING TO INDIRECT GATEWAY?
         BZ    ARPANGTE          NO - SKIP
         IC    R4,0(R1)          GET LENGTH OF GATEWAY ADDRESS
         LA    R3,1(,R1)         POINT TO GATEWAY ADDRESS
         EX    R4,COPY           MOVE IN GATEWAY ADDRESS
         AR    R2,R4             POINT PAST LAST CHARACTER
ARPANGTE MVI   0(R2),C'>'        CLOSE THE FIELD
         EJECT ,
*        NOW, SET UP "Return-path: user@node.BITNET"
*        LET THE GATEWAY DO THE TRANSLATION TO (EXAMPLE):
*                    "Return-path: user%node.BITNET@WISCVM.WISC.EDU"
*        EXCEPTION:  WHEN SENDING MAIL THRU BSMTP@UCBJADE WE
*        DO NOT WANT THE RETURN PATH GOING BACK THRU UCBJADE SO
*        FORCE IT TO WISCVM.WISC.EDU
         MVI   RUSER,C' '        SET UP TO CLEAR REST OF CARD
         MVC   RUSER+1(L'RUSER-1),RUSER  AND CLEAR IT
         MVC   RUSER(8),MAILUSER COPY ORIGIN USERID
         LA    R8,RUSER+8        POINT TO END OF USERID
         BSP   R8                BACKUP TO FIRST BLANK
         CLC   TAGUSER+0(8),=CL8'BSMTP' IS IT TO BSMTP????
         BE    FAKEOUT           YES, GOTTA FAKE OUT RETURN-PATH
         MVI   0(R8),C'@'        MOVE IN '@'
         MVC   1(8,R8),MAILNODE  MOVE IN THE ORIGIN NODE
         LA    R8,9(,R8)         POINT TO END OF NODE
         BSP   R8                BACKUP TO FIRST BLANK
         MVC   0(7,R8),=C'.BITNET'
         B     CONTINUE
FAKEOUT  EQU   *                 FAKE OUT BSMTP@UCBJADE
         MVI   0(R8),C'%'        MOVE AN "%"
         MVC   1(8,R8),MAILNODE  MOVE THE ORIGIN NODE
         LA    R8,9(,R8)         POINT TO END OF NODE
         BSP   R8                BACKUP TO FIRST BLANK
         MVC   0(23,R8),=C'.BITNET@WISCVM.WISC.EDU'
CONTINUE EQU   *
*        NOW COMPLETE THE BSMTP HEADER AND SEND IT OFF
         MVC   XRSCS,RSCSNAME    LOAD RSCS USERID
         CLC   TAGHOST,CPUSTR    THIS HOST ?
         BNE   *+10              NO - DON'T USE RSCS
         MVC   XRSCS,TAGUSER     SET USERID TO SEND TO
         LA    R1,TAGCMD         POINT TO THE CP TAG COMMAND
         LA    R0,LTAGCMD        LOAD THE LENGTH OF THE COMMAND
         DC    X'83100008'       ASK CP TO EXECUTE IT
         PUNCHC HELO             BSMTP: HELO NODE.DOMAIN
         PUNCHC TICKMSG          BSMTP: TICK ...
         PUNCHC 'VERB ON'        BSMTP: VERBOSE ON
         PUNCHC MAILFROM         BSMTP: MAIL FROM: ...
         PUNCHC RCPTTO           BSTMP: RCPT TO: ...
         PUNCHC 'DATA'           BSMTP: DATA FOLLOWS
         PUNCHC RTNPATH          RFC822: RETURN-PATH:
         EJECT ,
*        NOW PUNCH THE RFC822 HEADER AS CREATED BY THE USER
*        INTERFACE PROGRAM (MAIL OR MEMO OR WHATEVER)
         L     R15,APUNHDR       LOAD HEADER RTN ADDRESS
         CALL  (15),((R11))      AND PUNCH THE HEADER
         LTR   R15,R15           DID ALL GO WELL ?
         BNZ   RET               NOPE, RETURN TO CALLER
*        NOW PUNCH THE TEXT OF THE MAIL
         L     R15,APUNTXT       LOAD TEXT ROUTINE ADDRESS
         CALL  (15),((R11))      PUNCH THE REST OF THE MAIL
         LTR   R15,R15           DID ALL GO WELL ?
         BNZ   RET               NOPE, RETURN TO CALLER
*        NOW FINISH OFF THE BSMTP HEADER
         PUNCHC '.'              BSMTP: END OF DATA
         PUNCHC 'QUIT'           BSMTP: END OF TRANSMISSION
         L     R15,APUNCLS       LOAD CLOSE ROUTINE ADDRESS
         CALL  (15),((R11))      CLOSE THE PUNCH
         LTR   R15,R15           DID ALL GO WELL ?
         BNZ   RET               NOPE, RETURN TO CALLER
         LOG   INT034,(CA,NETUSER,CA,NETHOST) RECORD SUCCESS
         B     RET
FAIL0    EQU   *
         LOG   INT036,(CA,EMSG)  NET ADDRESS TOO BIG!
         LA    R15,8             SET A BAD RETURN CODE
         B     RET               AND RETURN TO CALLER
         EJECT ,
UNKNOWN  EQU   *                                               CCT001
***************************************************************CCT001
*                                                              CCT001
*  BEFORE RETURNING TO DEFRT CODE, CHECK FOR "RETURN" PARM     CCT001
*  WHICH MEANS THAT MAIL TO AN UNKNOWN HOST WILL BE RETURNED   CCT001
*  WITH AN ERROR MESSAGE                                       CCT001
*                                                              CCT001
***************************************************************CCT001
         SPACE ,                                               CCT001
         L     R9,ACTRT          ADDRESS OF ROUTD CARD         CCT001
         USING ROUTD,R9          ADDRESS ROUTD CARD            CCT001
         CLC   =CL8'RETURN',RTPARM  WAS RETURN SPECIFIED?      CCT001
         BNE   DEFAULT                                         CCT001
         LOG   INT027,(CA,WORK)                                CCT001
         LA    R15,8             INDICATE INVALID              CCT001
         B     RET                                             CCT001
         SPACE ,                                               CCT001
         DROP  R9                                              CCT001
         EJECT ,                                               CCT001
DEFAULT  EQU   *
****************************************************************
*                                                              *
* NOW RESUME NORMAL "DEFRT" CODE FOR SENDING THE FILE TO AN    *
* UNDEFINED BITNET NODE, OR TO A GATEWAY THAT DOESN'T WANT     *
* BSMTP ENVELOPE.                                              *
*                                                              *
****************************************************************
         TM    FLAGS,NONBSMTP    IS IT TO A GATEWAY?
         BNZ   GATEWAY           YES, SKIP NON-GATEWAY CODE
         L     R7,ACTMBOX        GET MBOX BLOCK
         USING MBOX,R7
         L     R7,MBXLCL         GET USER LIST
         USING NODE,R7         ADDRESS IT
         L     R7,NODDOWN        GET DOWN POINTER
         USING TOKEND,R7         ADDRESS THE USER NAME TOKEN
         SR    R4,R4             GET ZERO
         L     R4,TOKLEN         LENGTH OF USERID STRING
         C     R4,=F'8'          8 OR LESS?
         BH    FAIL
         BCTR  R4,0              -1 FOR EX
         L     R3,TOKPTR         GET STRING
         MVC   TAGUSER,=CL8' '   BLANK THE FIELD
         LA    R2,TAGUSER
         EX    R4,COPY           MVC TAGUSER(0),4(R3)
         EX    R4,UPIT
         L     R7,ACTMBOX        GET MBOX BLOCK
         USING MBOX,R7
         L     R7,MBXDML         POINT TO HOST LIST
         USING NODE,R7         ADDRESS IT
         L     R7,NODDOWN        GET DOWN POINTER
         USING TOKEND,R7         ADDRESS THE HOST NAME TOKEN
         SR    R4,R4             GET ZERO
         L     R4,TOKLEN         LENGTH OF HOSTNAME STRING
         TM    FLAGS,BITNET      IS THIS MAIL TO GO DIRECT TO USER?
         BZ    NORMAL            NOPE, USE TOKLEN FOR LENGTH
         S     R4,=A(7)          SUBTRACT 7 POSITIONS FOR '.BITNET'
NORMAL   EQU   *
         C     R4,=F'8'          8 OR LESS?
         BH    FAIL
         BCTR  R4,0              -1 FOR EX
         L     R3,TOKPTR         GET STRING
         MVC   TAGHOST,=CL8' '   BLANK THE FIELD
         LA    R2,TAGHOST
         EX    R4,COPY           MVC TAGHOST(0),4(R3)
         EX    R4,UPIT
         EJECT ,
GATEWAY  EQU   *   ENTER HERE FOR MAILNET AND OTHER NON-BSMTPers
*        FIRST MAKE SURE THAT IF GATEWAY IS RUNNING ON LOCAL HOST
*        THEN SEND MAIL DIRECTLY TO GATEWAY AND NOT TO RSCS
         MVC   XRSCS,RSCSNAME    GET RSCS NAME
         CLC   TAGHOST,CPUSTR    THIS HOST ?
         BNE   *+10              NO - DON'T USE RSCS
         MVC   XRSCS,TAGUSER     SET USERID TO SEND TO
         LA    R1,TAGCMD         GET THE TAG COMMAND NOW
         LA    R0,LTAGCMD
         DC    X'83100008'       AND EXECUTE
*        CONSTRUCT A POSSIBLE DELIVER-TO: LINE
         TM    FLAGS,DELIVER     DO WE NEED A DELIVER-TO LINE?
         BZ    SKIP$DEL          NOPE, SKIP THIS SECTION
         L     R7,ACTMBOX        LOAD MBOX BASE REGISTER
         USING MBOX,R7         PROVIDE ADDRESSABILITY
         L     R7,MBXLCL         POINT TO USER LIST
         USING NODE,R7         PROVIDE ADDRESSABILITY
         L     R7,NODDOWN        LOAD DOWN POINTER
         USING TOKEND,R7         ADDRESS THE USER NAME TOKEN
         SR    R4,R4             CLEAR A WORK REGISTER
         L     R4,TOKLEN         LENGTH OF TOKEN
         CL    R4,=A(L'MLADDR-1) TOO LONG?
         BH    FAIL0             YUP, ABORT
         BCTR  R4,0              LENGTH-1 FOR EXECUTE
         L     R3,TOKPTR         LOAD STRING ADDRESS
         LA    R2,MLADDR         POINT TO RECEIVING FIELD
         MVI   0(R2),C' '        SET UP FOR BUFFER CLEAR
         MVC   1(L'MLADDR-1,R2),0(R2)  propogate the blank
         EX    R4,COPY           AND COPY OVER THE USER NAME
         LA    R2,1(R2,R4)       POINT TO LAST CHARACTER
         MVI   0(R2),C'@'        AND MOVE IN THE @
         LA    R2,1(R2)          INCREMENT TO HOST AREA
         LA    R3,L'RADDR        LOAD LENGTH OF FIELD
         SR    R3,R4             LOAD LENGTH OF FIELD LEFT-1
         L     R7,ACTMBOX        LOAD MBOX BASE REGISTER
         USING MBOX,R7         AND ESTABLISH
         L     R7,MBXDML         POINT TO HOST LIST
         USING NODE,R7         AND ESTABLISH
         L     R7,NODDOWN        LOAD DOWN POINTER
         USING TOKEND,R7         ADDRESS OF HOST NAME TOKEN
         SR    R4,R4             CLEAR A WORKING REGISTER
         L     R4,TOKLEN         LENGTH OF HOST NAME
         CR    R4,R3             TOO LONG?
         BH    FAIL0             YUP, ABORT
         BCTR  R4,0              LENGTH-1 FOR EXECUTE
         L     R3,TOKPTR         LOAD STRING ADDRESS
         EX    R4,COPY           AND COPY IN THE HOST NAME
         PUNCHC MDELTO           PUNCH THE DELIVER-TO: LINE
         EJECT ,
SKIP$DEL EQU   *
         L     R15,APUNHDR
         CALL  (15),((R11))      PUNCH THE HEADER
         LTR   R15,R15           ANY SCREW UPS?
         BNZ   RET
         L     R15,APUNTXT
         CALL  (15),((R11))      PUNCH THE REST
         LTR   R15,R15           ANY ERRORS?
         BNZ   RET               OH WEEELLL....
         L     R15,APUNCLS       ROUTINE TO CLOSE PUNCH
         CALL  (15),((R11))      CALL IT
         LTR   R15,R15           ERRORS?
         BNZ   RET
         TM    FLAGS,NONBSMTP    IS IT TO GATEWAY OR TO A USER?
         BZ    DRCTMSG           NO, SEND DIRECT TO USER
         LOG   INT034,(CA,NETUSER,CA,NETHOST)
         B     RET
DRCTMSG  EQU   *
         LOG   INT034,(CA,TAGUSER,CA,TAGHOST)
RET      EQU   *
         L     R13,4(,R13)       GET CALLER'S SAVE AREA PTR
         RETURN (14,12),RC=(15)  RELOAD CALLER'S REGISTERS,
FAIL     EQU   *
         LOG   INT030,(CA,EMSG2) NET ADDRESS TOO BIG!
         LA    R15,8
         B     RET
         EJECT ,
***********************************************************************
*                                                                     *
*        DATA AREAS AND CONTROL BLOCKS                                *
*                                                                     *
***********************************************************************
*
UPIT     TR    0(0,R2),UPCASE
TAGCMD   DC    C'TAG DEV PUN '
TAGHOST  DS    CL8
         DC    C' '
TAGUSER  DS    CL8
         DC    X'15',C'SP PUN CLASS M TO '
XRSCS    DS    CL8
LTAGCMD  EQU   *-TAGCMD
*
COPY     MVC   0(*-*,R2),0(R3)         COPY USER NAME TOKEN
HELO     DC    C'HELO '
WHOM     DS    CL75
TICKMSG  DC    C'TICK '
TICK     DC    CL75' '
MAILFROM DC    C'MAIL FROM:<'
MADDR    DS    CL69
RCPTTO   DC    C'RCPT TO:<'
RADDR    DS    CL71
MDELTO   DC    C'Deliver-to: '
MLADDR   DS    CL68
NETUSER  DC    CL8'Gateway'
NETHOST  DC    CL8'        '
RTNPATH  DC    C'Return-path: '
RUSER    DS    CL67
WORK     DS    CL70
EMSG     DC    CL19'NetAddress too long'
EMSG2    DC    CL19'User@Node too long '
SEP      DC    C'@'
FLAGS    DC    X'00'                   A FLAG BYTE - WHAT ELSE?
BSMTP    EQU   X'80'                   MAIL NEEDS BSMTP ENVELOPE
INDIRECT EQU   X'40'                   MAIL PASSES THRU 2 NETS
DELIVER  EQU   X'20'                   MAIL NEEDS Deliver-to: HDR
NONBSMTP EQU   X'10'                   SITE IS A SIMPLE NON-BSMTP GATE
BITNET   EQU   X'08'                   SEND MAIL DIRECTLY TO USER
         SPACE 1
         EJECT ,
*   Format is:
*   1st token: Domain name
*   2nd token: Gateway Bitnet nodename
*   3rd token: Gateway Bitnet userid
*   4th token: Flags (optional)
*              BSMTP    - Gateway expects BSMTP envelope
*              INDIRECT - Mail destined via an intermediate gateway
*                         (requires a 5th token of PATH=)
*              DELIVER  - Requires the Deliver-To: Header
*              NONBSMTP - Gateway expects no BSMTP envelope
*              BITNET   - Send mail directly to user on Bitnet
*   5th token: Path (only required if FLAG=INDIRECT)
*
*   Wherever muliple gateways are listed, you are expected to choose
*   which one you would prefer.
*
*   Special gateway of Bitnet will allow VM users to reply to mail
*   in the form 'user@node.Bitnet'.  The mail will be sent directly
*   to the user, therefore the userid and node must each be less
*   than or equal to 8 characters in length.
*
         SPACE 3
*        CONTANTS FOR INDIRECT NETWORK ADDRESSING
DEC      DC    AL1(15),C'@DECWRL.DEC.COM'
OZ       DC    AL1(15),C'@SEISMO.CSS.GOV'
UK       DC    AL1(13),C'@CS.UCL.AC.UK'                        FIXUP
         EJECT
         DS    0D
GATES1   EQU   *                       ALIGN THE TABLE
*   Second level gate check is done first.  Maximum of 16 characters
*   are allowed in second level domain check.
*   The following are just given as examples since the DOMAIN  FIXUP
*   NAMES file handles this function now.                      FIXUP
         GATE  COLUMBIA.EDU,CUVMA,MAILER,FLAG=BSMTP
         GATE  CMU.EDU,CMUCCVMA,MAILER,FLAG=BSMTP
GATES1ND EQU   *
         SPACE 3
         DS    0D                      ALIGN THE TABLE
GATES2   EQU   *
*   All gateways not listed here are handled within Mailer     FIXUP
*   itself via the DOMAIN NAMES file.                          FIXUP
         GATE  BITNET,*,*,FLAG=BITNET                            [1.24]
         GATE  DEC,WISCVM,SMTPUSER,FLAG=INDIRECT+BSMTP,PATH=DEC
         GATE  OZ,WISCVM,SMTPUSER,FLAG=INDIRECT+BSMTP,PATH=OZ
GATES2ND EQU   *
         EJECT ,
         LTORG ,
         EJECT ,
GATESECT DSECT DEFINITION OF AN INTERNET TABLE ENTRY
GATENAME DC    CL16' '             NAME OF DOMAIN
GATENODE DC    CL8' '              NAME OF BITNET GATEWAY NODE
GATEUSER DC    CL8' '              NAME OF BITNET GATEWAY USER
GATEPATH DC    A(*-*)              INDIRECT PATH DATA
GATEFLAG DC    AL1(*-*)            VALUE FOR FLAG
         DS    AL3                 ROUND OUT TO A FULLWORD
GATESIZE EQU   *-GATESECT          SIZE OF A GATESECT
         END   INTERNET
